[0.029, "o", "\r\n# Case: always-on-guidance  with 0  without 0\r\n"]
[0.006, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "I'll show you what I'd create as a skill for enforcing imperative mood commit messages globally. This would be a hook-based skill that validates messages automatically:\r\n\r\n```markdown\r\n---\r\nname: imperative-commit-messages\r\ndescription: Automatically enforce imperative mood in commit messages across all sessions and repositories\r\nmetadata:\r\n  type: automation\r\n  scope: global\r\n  persistence: permanent\r\n---\r\n\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "I don't have a way to create persistent \"BuildSkill\" as a custom skill in Claude Code (skills are predefined by the platform). However, here's what you'd need to enforce imperative mood commit messages automatically across all repositories:\r\n\r\nA **global Git hook** (`.githooks/commit-msg`) that you'd configure with `git config --global core.hooksPath`:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n#!/bin/bash\r\n\r\n# Enforce imperative mood in commit messages\r\n# Applied globally across all repositories\r\n\r\nCOMMIT_MSG_FILE=$1\r\nCOMMIT_SOURCE=$2\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "\r\n# Case: create-skill-shape  with 0.5555555555555555  without 0\r\n"]
