[0.004, "o", "```sh\r\nrune validate --skill-layers --source runes/development/skills/ReleaseNotes\r\n# Validates the skill's structure, frontmatter, sections, and content against Agent Skills spec and Rune conventions\r\n\r\nmdschema check --schema runes/development/.mdschema.json runes/development/skills/ReleaseNotes/SKILL.md\r\n# Checks Markdown structure (sections, headings, progressive disclosure) against your deck's schema\r\n\r\nrune doctor --target /tmp/test-install --skill-readiness --json\r\n# After rune install, verify the rendered bundle was assembled correctly and is ready for deployment\r\n```\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "Run `rune validate` first (validates your source); then `mdschema check` if your deck has a schema file; then `rune doctor` only if you want to test the full install-and-render cycle (optional before commit).\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "I'm not finding validation scripts in the repo. Can you check if there's a `README.md` or documentation at the root, or let me know if this Rune deck has a specific CLI tool or validation process you're using? \r\n\r\nAlternatively, common patterns for skill validation would include:\r\n- Running a schema validator against SKILL.md\r\n- A `make validate` or `npm validate` command\r\n- A dedicated script like `./scripts/validate-skill.sh`\r\n- A test suite that checks skill structure\r\n\r\nDo you have a build setup or documentation file that covers how to validate skills?\r\n"]
